---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, SITE_NAMES } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title={`Cookies on ${SITE_NAMES[lang]}: none set, how to check`} description="Cookies on Benefit Sums: none on any page, and nothing about your benefits is stored on your device. Stability can be monitored without cookies, with your answers masked." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Cookies' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Cookies</h1>
    <p>This page completes the <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a>. You can check everything below in your browser’s developer tools, under Storage.</p>
    <h2>No cookies</h2><p>No page of the site sets a cookie, and the calculators store nothing on your device: earnings, rent, savings and the other answers you give stay in the open page and disappear when you close it. That is why there is no cookie banner: there is nothing to accept.</p>
    <h2>Anonymous stability monitoring</h2><p>To find pages that break, script errors, slow loading and buttons that fail, the site loads Microsoft Clarity in its cookie-free mode. Clarity then sets no cookie (no <code>_clck</code>, <code>_clsk</code>, <code>MUID</code> or <code>CLID</code>), gives every page view its own one-off identifier and does not link visits together. Page content and anything you type are masked before data is sent.</p>
    <h2>Blocking it</h2><p>Blocking the clarity.ms domain, or using a content blocker, stops this monitoring too; the calculators work just the same.</p>
    <p>Questions: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. Updated: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
